  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Committed a deterministic 25-row genus-2/3 oracle corpus with degrees 5-8, good/bad reduction, twists, generalized equations, characteristic 2, all p-ranks, supersingular/ordinary witnesses, local L-polynomials, first g extension counts, Jacobian orders/invariants, and odd-model Hasse-Witt matrices. Independent pure-Python exhaustive, Sage 10.9, PARI 2.17, and Magma 2.18 generators agree exactly where supported; Sage invariant factors reproduce Magma element-order histograms. Added offline arithmetic/provenance tests and a hashed cold/warm benchmark harness. Offline tests also pass on Linux arm64 and macOS arm64.",
    "risks": [
      "PARI hyperellcharpoly rejects the two generalized characteristic-2 cases; exhaustive Python, Sage, and Magma agree on them.",
      "The benchmark is an oracle-cost baseline on deliberately small exhaustive cases, not a production Sage.js throughput claim.",
      "The repository-wide test:native run was stopped at integration-owner request because simultaneous full builds saturated the shared host; focused oracle, strict-Python, and architecture receipts pass."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integration lane should consume local-data-v1.json for finite-field, Jacobian, smalljac, rforest, and genus-3 completion differential tests.",
      "Run repository-wide native and platform packaging suites once at final integration rather than duplicating them per data-only lane.",
      "Add large-prime or LMFDB rows only when a consumer needs a regression not represented by the compact exhaustive corpus."
    ]
  }
